# Measures a label through a vendored native library; the native code also writes a file of its own.
# NOT-LIKE-FOR-LIKE: CaMeL has no imports: the vendored nativefmt library reaches the plan as the measure tool, so the plan calls measure("report") instead of importing nativefmt, and the danger - the native code's own file write - is inside the library the tool runs, not in the plan.

print("length " + str(measure("report")))
